{
  "$comment": "Job cost corpus. The SPA (Classes/job.js) and the backend (models.Job.CostParts) both work out what a job cost, and both read these cases so the two cannot drift. Sale lines keep ESI's own field names (`tax`); our own aggregate is a transaction fee. Every component is summed from the rows that make it up: what a job produces from its setups, materials from each material's purchases, installs from the linked ESI jobs, extras from the extras rows and invention from its entries.",
